---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Logo from '../components/atoms/Logo.astro'
import Footer from '../components/organisms/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Insighty — Built for the Agencies Running on Spreadsheets"
  description="We built Insighty because we lived the problem — 40 clients, 30+ projects, and every tool fell short. Here is the real story."
>
  <main>

    <!-- =====================
    Custom About Header
    (minimal, full-width, transparent — blends into dark hero)
    ======================== -->
    <header class="dark absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 px-6 py-6 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/">
        <Logo class="w-[120px]" />
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <a href="/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white text-tagline-2 uppercase tracking-wider font-medium transition-colors hidden sm:block">← Back</a>
        <a href="/request-a-demo" class="btn btn-md btn-primary"><span>Request a demo</span></a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- =====================
    Hero — personal, not corporate
    ======================== -->
    <section
      class="relative min-h-[90vh] flex items-end pb-20 overflow-hidden"
      style="background: linear-gradient(160deg, #060d1e 0%, #0d1f42 55%, #162d60 100%)"
    >
      <!-- grid texture -->
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.035]" style="background-image: linear-gradient(#fff 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, #fff 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 40px 40px;"></div>

      <!-- subtle glow -->
      <div class="absolute top-1/3 right-1/4 w-[600px] h-[600px] rounded-full opacity-[0.06]" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #6e8fd9 0%, transparent 70%);"></div>

      <div class="main-container relative z-10">
        <div class="max-w-[800px] space-y-8">
          <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-medium text-white/30 border border-white/10 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full">The story</span>
          <h1 class="text-white leading-[1.1]">
            I managed 40 clients,<br />
            30+ projects, and tried<br />
            <span class="hero-text-gradient hero-text-color-1">every tool that existed.</span><br />
            None of them worked.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-white/55 text-tagline-1 max-w-[540px] leading-relaxed">
            So I built the one that did.
          </p>

          <!-- founder credit -->
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 pt-4 border-t border-white/10 max-w-[400px]">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-white/10 border border-white/15 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
              <span class="text-white/70 text-tagline-2 font-semibold">N</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white/80 text-tagline-2 font-medium">Nino Erjavec</p>
              <p class="text-white/35 text-tagline-3">Founder &amp; Digital Products Director</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =====================
    The real story — first person
    ======================== -->
    <section class="bg-background-1 dark:bg-background-8 py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="main-container">
        <div class="max-w-[680px] mx-auto space-y-10">
          <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-widest font-medium text-secondary/30 dark:text-accent/30">How it started</span>

          <div class="space-y-6 text-tagline-1 text-secondary/70 dark:text-accent/70 leading-[1.8]">
            <p class="text-secondary dark:text-accent text-[1.25rem] font-medium leading-relaxed">
              At the agency where I was Digital Products Director, we had 40 active clients and north of 30 projects running in parallel at any given time.
            </p>
            <p>
              That sounds manageable on paper. It is not. Not when delivery lives in Jira, revenue targets live in a Google Sheet, contracts live in a folder no one has organized since 2021, and the question "are we actually profitable this quarter?" takes three people half a day to answer.
            </p>
            <p>
              I am not someone who gives up on tools easily. I spent years trying to make it work — Asana, Monday, Teamwork, ClickUp, Harvest, custom Notion setups, spreadsheet automations. I benchmarked dozens of tools. I built internal processes around their limitations. I even customized some of them heavily to get closer to what we needed.
            </p>
            <p>
              The problem was never the tools themselves. The problem is structural: none of them were built for an agency. They were built for product teams, or for freelancers, or for enterprise procurement. Nobody built the one thing an agency operations director actually needs — a single view that connects revenue, projects, contracts, retainers, and infrastructure, and tells you what is at risk before it becomes a problem.
            </p>
            <p>
              So we built it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =====================
    The moment — dramatic beat
    ======================== -->
    <section class="bg-background-2 dark:bg-background-7 py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-stroke-2 dark:border-stroke-5">
      <div class="main-container">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 xl:gap-24 items-start">

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-widest font-medium text-secondary/30 dark:text-accent/30">The breaking point</span>
            <h2 class="text-secondary dark:text-accent">The Monday morning spreadsheet</h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 text-tagline-1 text-secondary/65 dark:text-accent/65 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                Every Monday, someone opened a spreadsheet to answer the same questions: what did we invoice last month, which retainers are renewing this quarter, which project is burning over budget right now.
              </p>
              <p>
                We had powerful tools. We had good processes. And we still could not answer basic operational questions without manual work.
              </p>
              <p>
                That was the moment. Not a dramatic failure — just the quiet realization that we were doing this every single week, and no tool was ever going to fix it unless it was actually designed for this specific problem.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- stats — honest ones -->
          <div class="space-y-4 lg:pt-12">
            {[
              { num: '40', label: 'clients managed', sub: 'Active clients across a full-service digital agency before building Insighty.' },
              { num: '30+', label: 'parallel projects', sub: 'Simultaneous projects in delivery — each with its own budget, timeline, and contract.' },
              { num: '27+', label: 'tools evaluated', sub: 'Every major agency tool benchmarked, tested, and customized before we gave up on finding one.' },
            ].map(stat => (
              <div class="rounded-2xl border border-stroke-2 dark:border-stroke-5 bg-background-1 dark:bg-background-6 p-7">
                <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
                  <span class="text-4xl font-bold text-secondary dark:text-accent">{stat.num}</span>
                  <span class="text-tagline-1 font-medium text-secondary/55 dark:text-accent/55">{stat.label}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-tagline-2 text-secondary/45 dark:text-accent/45 leading-relaxed">{stat.sub}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =====================
    Why existing tools failed
    ======================== -->
    <section class="bg-background-1 dark:bg-background-8 py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="main-container">
        <div class="max-w-[760px] space-y-10">
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-widest font-medium text-secondary/30 dark:text-accent/30">The real problem</span>
            <h2 class="text-secondary dark:text-accent">Every tool solved part of the problem.<br />None solved all of it.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            {[
              { tool: 'Project management tools', gap: 'Great for delivery. Blind to revenue, contracts, and what a project is actually costing the business.' },
              { tool: 'Time tracking tools', gap: 'Track hours. Can\'t tell you if a retainer is profitable or which client is burning your team.' },
              { tool: 'Accounting software', gap: 'Shows invoices sent. Has no concept of delivery progress, resource allocation, or project margin.' },
              { tool: 'CRM tools', gap: 'Pipeline management. Disconnected from the delivery reality once a deal is closed.' },
              { tool: 'Custom spreadsheets', gap: 'The actual workhorse. But manually maintained, always out of date, and impossible to act on in real time.' },
              { tool: 'All-in-one platforms', gap: 'Feature-complete for generic teams. Missing the agency-specific workflows that are not negotiable.' },
            ].map(item => (
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-stroke-2 dark:border-stroke-5 bg-background-2 dark:bg-background-7 p-5 space-y-2">
                <p class="text-tagline-2 font-semibold text-secondary dark:text-accent">{item.tool}</p>
                <p class="text-tagline-2 text-secondary/50 dark:text-accent/50 leading-relaxed">{item.gap}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-2 border-stroke-3 dark:border-stroke-4 pl-6">
            <p class="text-tagline-1 text-secondary/70 dark:text-accent/70 leading-relaxed italic">
              "The gap was not about features. It was about the mental model. No tool was built around the way an agency actually operates — the intersection of delivery, revenue, contracts, and client relationships as one living system."
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =====================
    What we built
    ======================== -->
    <section class="bg-background-2 dark:bg-background-7 py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-stroke-2 dark:border-stroke-5">
      <div class="main-container space-y-12">
        <div class="max-w-[580px] space-y-3">
          <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-widest font-medium text-secondary/30 dark:text-accent/30">What we built</span>
          <h2 class="text-secondary dark:text-accent">Six surfaces. One source of truth.</h2>
          <p class="text-tagline-1 text-secondary/60 dark:text-accent/60 leading-relaxed">
            Each surface answers a different question your agency asks every week. Together, they replace the spreadsheets and connect the tools you already use.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
          {[
            { title: 'Revenue hub', body: 'Every income stream in one matrix — projects, retainers, hosting, domains, and pipeline. Weekly targets. Monthly actuals. No more guessing.' },
            { title: 'Project management', body: 'Delivery tracking with budget burn visibility. Know which projects are profitable and which are bleeding margin, in real time.' },
            { title: 'Contract management', body: 'Contracts, SLAs, and change requests — tracked against billing status so nothing slips and no renewal is ever missed.' },
            { title: 'Maintenance billing', body: 'Monthly and annual retainers with included hours, bug allowances, and automated recurring invoicing built in.' },
            { title: 'Infrastructure registry', body: 'Every hosting account, domain, and SSL certificate — with automated renewal alerts at 90, 60, and 30 days.' },
            { title: 'Pixel AI', body: 'Proactive intelligence that surfaces anomalies and flags risks before you think to look. The Monday morning spreadsheet, automated.' },
          ].map(item => (
            <div class="bg-background-1 dark:bg-background-6 rounded-2xl border border-stroke-2 dark:border-stroke-5 p-6 space-y-2">
              <p class="text-tagline-1 font-semibold text-secondary dark:text-accent">{item.title}</p>
              <p class="text-tagline-2 text-secondary/60 dark:text-accent/60 leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =====================
    CTA
    ======================== -->
    <section class="bg-background-1 dark:bg-background-8 py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="main-container">
        <div class="max-w-[580px] space-y-6">
          <span class="inline-block text-tagline-3 uppercase tracking-widest font-medium text-secondary/30 dark:text-accent/30">Join us early</span>
          <h2 class="text-secondary dark:text-accent">Built with agencies who live this problem daily</h2>
          <p class="text-tagline-1 text-secondary/60 dark:text-accent/60 leading-relaxed">
            Insighty is pre-launch. We are onboarding a small group of founding members who will shape the product, lock in pre-launch pricing, and run on Insighty before the world does.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-2">
            <a href="/founding-member" class="btn btn-md btn-primary"><span>Become a founding member</span></a>
            <a href="/request-a-demo" class="btn btn-md btn-secondary dark:btn-accent"><span>Request a demo</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
